  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 114 PM MDT Mon Sep 14 2026\n\nCool temperatures remain in place today behind frontal system \nthat passed through this weekend. Winds remain breezy as well, \nbut overall impact will be greatest overnight as lows fall to \ncoldest of the week. NBM retains a wide swath of sub-36 degree \nlows across the Snake River Plain, but traditional NAM and GFS \nguidance puts temperatures slightly cooler than NBM, closer to \npotential freeze. Will maintain the Frost Advisory across much \nof the Snake River Plain, and note that the interstate corridor \nthrough the Snake Plain will likely be a few degrees warmer than\nthresholds of concern, but that shifts cooler moving north of \nIdaho Falls.\n\nTemperatures shift warmer through the week as ridge rebuilds\nahead of next incoming low pressure feature, poised to arrive\nmid week. Models have been shifting precipitation chances\naround, and are seeing a signal for increased moisture as early\nas Wednesday afternoon/evening across the southern and eastern\nhighlands. The threat for showers and thunderstorms increases\nWednesday night through Friday, possibly continuing into early\nSaturday as the low shifts across East Idaho.",
